Project: Glitch, a 3D web3 city game for the NEAR Hackathon https://nearhackathon.com/ (Track 09, Games With Real Economies).
Stack: TypeScript everywhere. web/ = Vite + three.js. server/ = Node + Hono. shared/ = pure TS used by both.
Hard rules:
1. The browser never decides money. The server computes and validates every game result before minting or burning on NEAR.
2. Players never see wallets, gas or signing. Only the advertiser page uses a wallet.
3. All randomness is seeded (mulberry32) so fast-forward is deterministic.
4. Game rules live in readable files: shared/merchants.rules.ts and shared/events.rules.ts.
5. Network: NEAR testnet only. Contract addresses and keys come from env vars, never hardcoded.
6. Keep dependencies minimal. Explain any new dependency in one line.
Original single-file prototype: legacy/glitch-prototype-v2c.html (reference only, do not delete).